editorialMd:
The working idea

Split the line into maximal runs of non-space ASCII characters and produce each run's length. Multiple spaces, leading spaces and trailing spaces do not produce empty words.

Return the weighted sum of the derived sequence: multiply its first value by 1, its second by 2, and so on, then add the products. Return 0 for an empty sequence.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(n); space O(n).

javascript
function wordSlipsBossReceipt(line, k) {
  const a=line; let out=[];
  let length=0;for(let i=0;i<=a.length;i++){if(i===a.length||a[i]===' '){if(length)out.push(length);length=0;}else length++;}
  return out.reduce((s,x,i)=>s+(i+1)*x,0);
}


